{
  "an1.394:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 1.394–574 ",
  "an1.394:0.2": "Another Chapter on a Finger-Snap ",
  "an1.394:1.0": "394 ",
  "an1.394:1.1": "“If, mendicants, a mendicant develops the first absorption, even as long as a finger-snap, they are called ",
  "an1.394:1.2": "a mendicant who does not lack absorption, who follows the Teacher’s instructions, who responds to advice, and who does not eat the country’s alms in vain. ",
  "an1.394:1.3": "How much more so those who make much of it!” ",
  "an1.395:1.0": "395–401 ",
  "an1.395:1.1": "“If, mendicants, a mendicant develops the second … ",
  "an1.396:1.1": "third … ",
  "an1.397:1.1": "or fourth absorption … ",
  "an1.398:1.1": "or the heart’s release by love … ",
  "an1.399:1.1": "or the heart’s release by compassion … ",
  "an1.400:1.1": "or the heart’s release by rejoicing … ",
  "an1.401:1.1": "or the heart’s release by equanimity, even as long as a finger-snap …” ",
  "an1.402:1.0": "402–405 ",
  "an1.402:1.1": "“If a mendicant meditates by observing an aspect of the body … ",
  "an1.403:1.1": "feelings … ",
  "an1.404:1.1": "mind … ",
  "an1.405:1.1": "principles—keen, aware, and mindful, rid of covetousness and displeasure for the world, even for the time of a finger-snap …” ",
  "an1.406:1.0": "406–409 ",
  "an1.406:1.1": "“If they generate enthusiasm, try, make an effort, exert the mind, and strive so that bad, unskillful qualities don’t arise, even for the time of a finger-snap … ",
 